     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "たら introduces a condition and can also introduce what will be done when something happens.",
     "texto": [
      "The form is the short past + ら: 雨が降ったら. It doesn't mean the action has happened; the context may be talking about a future possibility.",
      "あめ が ふったら、 うち に います。 (If it rains, I'll stay at home.)",
      "えき に ついたら、 れんらく して ください。 (When you arrive at the station, please let me know.)"
     ],
